From 23032d4b04d1d1a54182ca10f762f022075b7358 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Evolution BR811 <344454957+Evolution-BR811@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:43:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VGM import: YM2413 (MSX-MUSIC, Master System FM) and VRC7

- notes are key ons; the chip's own envelope plays them
- preset patches go to the instrument (wave macro when the patch changes
  inside a note), the custom patch becomes the instrument's operators
- changes to the custom patch during a note become FM macros of the
  note that owns it; a key on inside a row becomes a phase reset macro
- rhythm mode imports as "OPLL with drums" (18xx when it is switched)
- pitch matched exactly through Furnace's own f-num calculation
- works alongside the SN76489 (Master System FM) and the 2A03 (VRC7)
- leading silent ticks are no longer added before the first write

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KMJUrc1fn7dir5w2PfSPK2
